;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljk:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; FOUR independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system (the entity record, the RA000602 entry in the
;;     registration-authorities registry, the XTIQ entry in the entity-legal-forms
;;     registry, and the LEI record of the managing LOU)
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (the ACTIVE NASDAQ
;;     filer, CIK 0001468328 -- 10-K, 10-Q, 8-K, DEF 14A)
;;   * the State of Delaware, via the Division of Corporations portal at
;;     corp.delaware.gov -- the very register RA000602 names (portal only; see
;;     below for why no per-entity row exists)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its corporate site and at the exact Terms-of-Use
;;     page this repository archives in 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;
;; HOW GLEIF AND DELAWARE ARE LINKED -- BY SHARED KEY, RESOLVED ONE WAY ONLY.
;; GLEIF names RA000602 (Division of Corporations, Department of State,
;; Delaware) as both register of record and validation authority, and records
;; registeredAs 4196548 and validatedAs 4196548 -- the Delaware file number.
;; The same digits reappear inside GLEIF's OpenCorporates pointer
;; ocid us_de/4196548 (row gleif-ocid). But unlike Japan's NTA in the sibling
;; NTT catalog, Delaware exposes NO stable public per-entity URL: the ICIS
;; entity search at icis.corp.delaware.gov is form-gated. So the file number
;; can be READ OUT of GLEIF but not RESOLVED at the register itself by this
;; gate -- the corp.delaware.gov rows are :definition (the register exists),
;; not :identity (the register names this entity).
;;
;; HOW GLEIF AND THE SEC ARE LINKED -- BY ATTRIBUTES, NOT BY KEY. EDGAR still
;; carries "lei":null for this filer (row sec-lei-null, which goes red the day
;; EDGAR starts printing the LEI, at which point a direct-key row should
;; replace it). The link is: the name (ADDUS HOMECARE CORPORATION / Addus
;; HomeCare Corp), the state of incorporation DE (row sec-state-of-inc,
;; matching GLEIF's jurisdiction US-DE), and the headquarters city FRISCO,
;; TX 75034 -- attributes in agreement, no register quoting another.
;;
;; THE STALE ADDRESS, RECORDED HONESTLY. GLEIF's registration status is LAPSED
;; (row gleif-registration-lapsed): nextRenewalDate passed 2020-02-22 and the
;; record was last updated 2021-07-15. GLEIF's headquarters row still reads
;; 6801 Gaylord Parkway, Suite 110, Frisco TX 75034 (row gleif-hq-street).
;; EDGAR, kept current by the filer's own submissions, reads 6303 COWBOYS WAY,
;; SUITE 600, FRISCO TX 75034 (rows sec-street, sec-city, sec-zip). Same city,
;; same ZIP, different street: the company moved and the lapsed GLEIF record
;; never followed. Both are cited BECAUSE they disagree -- the disagreement is
;; itself a dated, verifiable fact about register freshness, and either row
;; going red signals one register catching up.
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's nextRenewalDate is frozen in the
;; lapsed record and would prove nothing but the lapse already pinned by row
;; gleif-registration-lapsed. NASDAQ's own quote page for ADUS is JS-rendered
;; with no stable server-rendered bytes, so the listing is instead proven
;; directly at EDGAR (rows sec-ticker, sec-exchange) -- a direct proof the
;; sibling NTT catalog could not make for its TSE ticker. OpenCorporates
;; blocks unauthenticated fetches; row gleif-ocid pins only GLEIF's POINTER at
;; it, not the OpenCorporates page. The IRS has no public per-EIN URL, so EIN
;; 20-5340172 is proven at EDGAR only (row sec-ein). The ICIS per-entity
;; extract is form-gated (see above). The EDGAR body also carries a filings
;; list that changes with every filing; rows target only stable header fields.
;; The registered agent c/o CORPORATION SERVICE COMPANY, 251 LITTLE FALLS
;; DRIVE, WILMINGTON (rows gleif-registered-agent, gleif-legal-city) is CSC's
;; address, shared with thousands of Delaware registrants -- both rows are
;; :attribute, not :identity, for exactly that reason.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before
;; the claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or its seat.
;;               Point the URL at a different company and the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT
;;               (status ACTIVE, city FRISCO, SIC 8082, a registered-agent
;;               address shared across a state). Such a row can survive a swap
;;               to a similar company. It is recorded because it corroborates,
;;               not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the substring resolves a code or body the entity record points
;;               at (RA000602, XTIQ, the managing LOU, the registry portal). It
;;               says the named register, legal form or LOU exists; it says
;;               nothing about Addus by itself.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 14 are :identity, 20 are :attribute and 8 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 42 as identifying would overstate what
;; this catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body (GLEIF JSON escapes forward
;; slashes, so rows over URLs and the ocid pin the literal backslash-slash
;; bytes; EDGAR JSON is compact ASCII; the issuer HTML serves UTF-8 with
;; typographic quotes, pinned as-is) and were each checked against the fetched
;; bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22).
